Two of these deserve attention before anyone redistributes a build of this software:

  - **PySide6 is copyleft** (LGPL-3.0 / GPL). It supplies the GUI only; the embeddings
    layer and the headless CLI (`biofilm-embeddings-run`) do not require it at runtime
    beyond a module-level import in the shared row-collection helpers. A distribution
    that ships the GUI carries LGPL obligations that the rest of this list does not.
  - **imageio-ffmpeg** is BSD-2 itself but obtains an FFmpeg binary, whose license
    depends on how that binary was built (LGPL or GPL). It is used for overlay videos in
    the processing phase, not for embedding extraction.


Processing engine
-----------------
Image processing is provided by biofilm-processing, pinned as a git submodule at
external/biofilm-processing and installed from there.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/BridgesLabCMU/uPULLI-I
  Version:   v1.0.1 (the pinned tag)
  Copyright: (c) 2026 Carnegie Mellon University
  License:   Apache License 2.0 -- same terms as this package

Cloning this repository with --recurse-submodules produces a checkout of the engine at
external/biofilm-processing carrying its own LICENSE and NOTICE. Those files are the
engine's; they are not superseded by this package's copies at the repository root.

Note for anyone reading the paper: the published embeddings were produced under the
engine's v1.0.0, which was MIT. v1.0.1 changes licensing and package metadata only --
`git diff v1.0.0 v1.0.1` touches no file under src/ -- so the render is identical and
the pin move does not affect reproducibility of the published results.
